    {
      "n": 7,
      "sourceEntry": 1368,
      "speaker": "PARKES",
      "kind": "spoken",
      "text": "I see. I didn’t want to go home. But you all wanted to go because of a little rain. So I said we’d go. Then you didn’t want to go. You wanted to stay and be nice. So I was nice. Which was very hard. Then you wanted to go again. Now the bloody caravan is sinking into the mud and you want to stay! I’ll never understand women.",
      "src": "audio/pages/84/lines/007_parkes_b0a87ad1fb5_norm.mp3",
      "duration": 19.505,
      "speed": null,
      "voiceName": "Dave - Expressive Australian English"
